## Verdict — path-A memory floor
| Result | Meaning |
|--------|---------|
| **FAIL** | Advertised multi-import size rails are **not honest end-to-end**; large multi DoS/thrash is product-real; 150-module self-check is not a memory floor pass. |

**PASS slices (kept):** root **64KiB** gate fires; tiny multi-import check works; ambient List quota + ARC prevent unbounded *process* heap growth on short hangs (RSS flat while CPU burns).

**FAIL slices:** import-path **64KiB claim false**; **1MiB expanded** practically unreachable before thrash; **O(n²)** load/lex and superlinear multi-module RSS/time; oodac **150-module / ~832 KiB** self-check times out; `"\0"` import check compiled as digit **`0`** (false reject).

Residual R4/R5 in `ooda/bootstrap/AUDIT_RESIDUAL.oot` remains accurate — this audit **measures** them.

