## H1 — Expanded 1MiB limit honesty
### Code claims
| Site | Claim / gate | Limit |
|------|----------------|-------|
| `main.oo` | per-file before read; comment: “lex is O(n²) char_at — 64KiB max” | `file_size(root) > 65536` → `ERR load source exceeds 64KiB per-file limit` |
| `check_drive.oo` | “H6: expanded source bound (import concat); per-file is 64KiB at load” | `chars_len(src) > 1048576` → `ERR check source exceeds 1MiB expanded limit` |
| `check_mod.oo` | same expanded message on module body | 1048576 |
| `lex.oo` | `lex_all` | `n > 1048576` → Err `"source exceeds 1MiB limit"` |
| `load_import.oo` | DFS concat imports → one expanded `String` | **no size gate** on import files or running expanded size |

### Measurements
| Probe | Result | time | maxrss |
|-------|--------|------|--------|
| Root file 70000 B (`a`×70000) | **FAIL-CLOSED** `ERR load source exceeds 64KiB per-file limit` | 0.00 s | 3840 KB |
| Root small + import **70043 B** (`// x`×70000) | **No 64KiB reject** — `timeout 3` **124** (CPU thrash) | ≥3 s | ~7 MB |
| Multi expand **~1.03 MiB** (18×~60 KiB alpha modules, no digit `0` in names) | **timeout 20 s** — never printed 1MiB ERR | 20.00 s | 10468 KB |
| Multi expand **~0.80 MiB** (14 modules) | **timeout 15 s** — under limit, still hang | 15.01 s | 8036 KB |
| oodac `main.oo` expand (see H3) | **831.8 KiB < 1 MiB** — hang without limit trip | ≥20–30 s | see H3 |

### Honesty scorecard
| Claim | Live truth | Score |
|-------|------------|-------|
| Root ≤64 KiB | Enforced on **entry path only** | **PASS** |
| “Per-file is 64KiB at load” (imports) | `load_expand` / `read_file` **no** `file_size` gate | **FAIL (dishonest comment)** |
| Expanded ≤1 MiB | Gate exists **after** full concat + only if check is reached | **PARTIAL code / FAIL practical** |
| 1 MiB protects multi trees | Load/lex **O(n²)** thrash dominates; 0.8–1.0 MiB multi **times out first** | **FAIL as safety rail** |
| Single-file 1 MiB lex path | Unreachable: root blocked at 64 KiB first | **N/A (dead rail for monofile)** |

**H1 residual (OK if documented):** true per-import 64 KiB in `load_expand`; running expanded byte counter abort before O(n²) concat; or incremental/per-file check (R5 close).

