## H3 — List/token memory on 150-module oodac tree
### Tree facts (static)
| Metric | Value |
|--------|------:|
| Modules reachable from `ooda/oodac/main.oo` | **150** |
| Sum of `.oo` bytes (approx expand) | **851740** (~**831.8 KiB**) |
| Under advertised 1 MiB expand? | **yes** (limit does not trip) |
| Any single file >64 KiB? | **0** (largest ~13.7 KiB `check_cap_util.oo`) |

### Live product check
| Command | Wall | maxrss / samples | Exit |
|---------|------|------------------|------|
| `timeout 20 oodac check ooda/oodac/main.oo` | 20 s | VmRSS **flat ~2268 KB** for 19 samples | **124** |
| `timeout 30 oodac check ooda/oodac/main.oo` | 30 s | maxrss **92508 KB** (prior sample) | **124** |
| `timeout 15 oodac tokens ooda/oodac/main.oo` | 15 s | maxrss **84020 KB** | **124** |

Interpretation:
- Early phase is **CPU-bound expand/lex thrash** (low RSS if ARC churns temps).
- Longer runs can climb to **~80–90 MB** without finishing — token materialization / bind strings if load progresses.
- **No OK** within 30 s; aligns with AUDIT_RESIDUAL **R4** (“>120s”) / **R5**.

### Token / list model
- `tokenize_lines` → `collect_tokens`: `List[String]` of TSV `kind\tline\tcol\text` rows; grows with every token.
- `list_push` path allocates new list buffers under ambient quota (`chs_rt_list.c`, default **64 MiB** ambient; `OO_LIST_AMBIENT_QUOTA`).
- Check path does **not** free `toks` explicitly after passes; process exit reclaims. Short CLI lifetime mitigates (R6 residual honesty).
- For N=80 tiny multi, **143 MB** RSS with only **5.6 KB** source shows list+string **constant factors** and multi-pass retention dominate.

**H3 residual:** per-file tokenize + merge symbols; stream tokens; drop intermediate lists; raise honesty that full expanded check of oodac is **not** path-A green.


